      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "1",
        "image": ""
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: The Sandmeyer reaction involves treating a diazonium salt with cuprous chloride (Cu2Cl2/HCl) or cuprous bromide (Cu2Br2/HBr) to prepare chlorobenzene (II) and bromobenzene (III). Fluorobenzene (I) is prepared via Balz-Schiemann, and iodobenzene (IV) via KI heating. Hence, exactly 2 can be prepared. Option A.",
