    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "question": "Choose the correct evaluation mapping of the halogen which is most reactive towards SN1 reaction in the pairs A, B, C, D shown in the diagram: (see diagram)",
    "questionImage": "halo easy/halo_easy_q3.png",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "A - Br(a); B - I(a); C - Br(b); D - Br(a)",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "A - Br(b); B - I(b); C - Br(b); D - Br(b)",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "A - Br(b); B - I(a); C - Br(a); D - Br(a)",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "A - Br(a); B - I(a); C - Br(a); D - Br(a)",
        "image": ""
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: In pair A, benzylic Br(a) is more reactive than secondary Br(b). In B, allylic I(a) is more reactive than vinylic I(b) (which is inert). In C, secondary Br(b) is reactive while bridgehead Br(a) is inert. In D, tertiary Br(a) is more reactive than primary Br(b). Hence A - Br(a); B - I(a); C - Br(b); D - Br(a). Option A.",
    "explanationImage": "",
